# ⛔ THIS FILE EXISTS TO OVERRIDE THE REPOSITORY-ROOT .vercelignore. Do not delete it.
#
# blackbox-supply-site is git-connected to the ascension-system monorepo with Root Directory
# `venture-harness/content-engine/site`. Vercel looks for .vercelignore in the project's root
# directory first and only falls back to the repository root - and the repository-root one ends
# with:
#
#     venture-harness/content-engine
#
# That line is CORRECT for the Ascension app, which deploys from the repo root and must not carry
# this venture with it. But applied to THIS project it deletes the site's own source before the
# build: the log read "Removed 3842 ignored files defined in .vercelignore", then "Installing
# dependencies... up to date in 426ms" (nothing to install, because package.json was gone), then
# "No Next.js version detected". Two production builds failed at 17s that way.
#
# So the fix is a project-local .vercelignore, not an edit to the shared root one - editing that
# would start dragging ~3,800 venture files into every Ascension deploy.

node_modules
.next
.vercel
*.log
